Relevant columns and their potential use  

• “IDC”.“IDC_V17”.“DICOM_PIVOT”  
  – “StudyInstanceUID”:  UID we finally need to count (DISTINCT).  
  – “SeriesInstanceUID”:  key that identifies each imaging series.  
  – “SeriesDescription”:   human‑readable text that lets us pick out  
     • “DWI”,  
     • “T2 Weighted Axial”,  
     • “Apparent Diffusion Coefficient”.  
  – “collection_id”:       must equal ‘qin_prostate_repeatability’.  

• “IDC”.“IDC_V17”.“SEGMENTATIONS”  
  – “segmented_SeriesInstanceUID”:  Series that was segmented (links back to DICOM_PIVOT.SeriesInstanceUID).  
  – “SeriesInstanceUID”:            the segmentation series itself.  
  – “StudyInstanceUID”:             inherits the study in which the segmentation lives.  
  – “TrackingUID”, “SegmentNumber”… : not essential here but useful for QA.  

Typical conditions to locate the series of interest  

1. DICOM_PIVOT.“collection_id” = ‘qin_prostate_repeatability’  
2. DICOM_PIVOT.“SeriesDescription” ILIKE ‘%DWI%’  
3. DICOM_PIVOT.“SeriesDescription” ILIKE ‘%T2%Weighted%Axial%’  
4. DICOM_PIVOT.“SeriesDescription” ILIKE ‘%Apparent%Diffusion%Coefficient%’  
5. SEGMENTATIONS.“SeriesInstanceUID” or SEGMENTATIONS.“segmented_SeriesInstanceUID” must map to a T2‑Weighted Axial series (join back to DICOM_PIVOT).

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (all limited to 20 rows) that build up from simple inspection to the final combined query.  
Remember to replace LIMIT 20 by LIMIT 20 OFFSET … if you want to page through more rows.

```sql
-- 1️⃣  See how many different series descriptions exist in the collection
SELECT DISTINCT "SeriesDescription"
FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_PIVOT"
WHERE "collection_id" = 'qin_prostate_repeatability'
LIMIT 20;

-- 2️⃣  Quick look at typical DWI series in that collection
SELECT "StudyInstanceUID",
       "SeriesInstanceUID",
       "SeriesDescription"
FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_PIVOT"
WHERE "collection_id" = 'qin_prostate_repeatability'
  AND "SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%DWI%'
LIMIT 20;

-- 3️⃣  Inspect T2‑Weighted Axial series
SELECT "StudyInstanceUID",
       "SeriesInstanceUID",
       "SeriesDescription"
FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_PIVOT"
WHERE "collection_id" = 'qin_prostate_repeatability'
  AND "SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%T2%Weighted%Axial%'
LIMIT 20;

-- 4️⃣  Inspect Apparent Diffusion Coefficient (ADC) series
SELECT "StudyInstanceUID",
       "SeriesInstanceUID",
       "SeriesDescription"
FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_PIVOT"
WHERE "collection_id" = 'qin_prostate_repeatability'
  AND "SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%Apparent%Diffusion%Coefficient%'
LIMIT 20;

-- 5️⃣  Distinct StudyInstanceUIDs for each of the three MR series types separately
SELECT DISTINCT "StudyInstanceUID"
FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_PIVOT"
WHERE "collection_id" = 'qin_prostate_repeatability'
  AND (
        "SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%DWI%' OR
        "SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%T2%Weighted%Axial%' OR
        "SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%Apparent%Diffusion%Coefficient%'
      )
LIMIT 20;

-- 6️⃣  Look at segmentation series in the study (raw list)
SELECT "StudyInstanceUID",
       "SeriesInstanceUID",
       "segmented_SeriesInstanceUID",
       "SegmentAlgorithmType"
FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."SEGMENTATIONS"
WHERE "SeriesInstanceUID" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;

-- 7️⃣  Join segmentation to its parent image series to see description
SELECT s."StudyInstanceUID",
       s."SeriesInstanceUID"          AS "SegSeries",
       s."segmented_SeriesInstanceUID" AS "ParentSeries",
       p."SeriesDescription"
FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."SEGMENTATIONS" s
JOIN "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_PIVOT"   p
  ON p."SeriesInstanceUID" = s."segmented_SeriesInstanceUID"
WHERE p."collection_id" = 'qin_prostate_repeatability'
LIMIT 20;

-- 8️⃣  Filter segmentation series that originate from T2‑Weighted Axial parent
SELECT DISTINCT s."StudyInstanceUID"
FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."SEGMENTATIONS" s
JOIN "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_PIVOT" p
  ON p."SeriesInstanceUID" = s."segmented_SeriesInstanceUID"
WHERE p."collection_id" = 'qin_prostate_repeatability'
  AND p."SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%T2%Weighted%Axial%'
LIMIT 20;

-- 9️⃣  All studies containing at least one of the four requested series categories
SELECT DISTINCT p."StudyInstanceUID"
FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_PIVOT" p
WHERE p."collection_id" = 'qin_prostate_repeatability'
  AND (
        p."SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%DWI%' OR
        p."SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%T2%Weighted%Axial%' OR
        p."SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%Apparent%Diffusion%Coefficient%'
      )
UNION
SELECT DISTINCT s."StudyInstanceUID"
FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."SEGMENTATIONS" s
JOIN "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_PIVOT" p
  ON p."SeriesInstanceUID" = s."segmented_SeriesInstanceUID"
WHERE p."collection_id" = 'qin_prostate_repeatability'
  AND p."SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%T2%Weighted%Axial%'
LIMIT 20;

-- 🔟  Count the UNIQUE StudyInstanceUIDs matching ALL criteria (remove LIMIT when ready)
SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT id)
FROM (
      SELECT p."StudyInstanceUID" AS id
      FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_PIVOT" p
      WHERE p."collection_id" = 'qin_prostate_repeatability'
        AND (
              p."SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%DWI%' OR
              p."SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%T2%Weighted%Axial%' OR
              p."SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%Apparent%Diffusion%Coefficient%'
            )
      UNION
      SELECT s."StudyInstanceUID"  AS id
      FROM "IDC"."IDC_V17"."SEGMENTATIONS" s
      JOIN "IDC"."IDC_V17"."DICOM_PIVOT" p
        ON p."SeriesInstanceUID" = s."segmented_SeriesInstanceUID"
      WHERE p."collection_id" = 'qin_prostate_repeatability'
        AND p."SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%T2%Weighted%Axial%'
     ) all_ids
LIMIT 20;
```
